ttered, ranging from a September survey showing a close contest to earlier polls giving Risch leads of 20 points or more. Still, the structural picture is consistent: Idaho leans Republican by about 18 points, every major race rater calls the seat Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Risch a 92 to 95 percent chance of winning. Achilles's path would require consolidating nearly all non-Republican voters plus a slice of moderates, a tall order in this state.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0421, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0261, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.0}]}